      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-team-2008-p1.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If 4 were juicy, then we would have \\(1=\\ldots+\\frac{1}{4}\\). The \\(\\ldots\\) can only possible contain \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\), but it is clear that \\(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\), and \\(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\) are all not equal to 1 .",
